  "limitations": "Java coverage belongs to launcher, not a shell percentage. Parent OS flock/inactive/backup/run binding, root-owned environment validation/publication, actual unit credential provisioning and timeout/TERM behavior, full batch, NK CHR and IT/ST are NOT certified. LinuxFileLock is a low-level capability only; root/type/UID/ACL/stable-namespace admission and parent lifecycle are not supplied by it. CLOEXEC is asserted at the native call boundary, not an actual inherited-FD inspection; aarch64 ABI selection only, execution is amd64. MaintenanceFileLock PT uses synthetic root UID/GID/tmpfs admission over real isolated unprivileged files. Actual root/tmpfiles provisioning and parent inactive/backup/DB handoff remain unverified. STOP is read-only transient state observation, not service stopping or a lease. Deployed units, root execution, parent restart prohibition/cgroup validation and integration remain unverified. Trusted fixed systemctl/OS assumptions apply; timeout is tested using a process fault port, not a real stalled manager or TERM-ignoring descendant.",
